    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d503">

                <pb facs="0656" n="644" sameAs="frus:frus1946v07/pg644"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867N.01/7–946: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The British Prime Minister</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Attlee</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to President Truman </hi><anchor
                        n="99" xml:id="d503-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-07-08">8 July, 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Personal and Top Secret. Many thanks for your telegram of July 6th [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">5th</hi>] and for action you have taken to expedite the
                    departure of your committee and their staff. We shall all here be ready for
                    discussions to begin on Friday next.</p>
                <p>I shall be delighted to see Ambassador Grady and Mr. Dorr upon their arrival and
                    have asked Averell<anchor n="1" xml:id="d503-f2"/> to let me know immediately
                    they arrive.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d503-f1" n="99" type="source" xml:id="d503-f1-content">
                <p>Copy transmitted to Mr. Acheson by Lord Inverchapel on July 9.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d503-f2" n="1" xml:id="d503-f2-content">
                <p>Ambassador Harriman.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
